+\subsection{Historical Provenance Audit of the Inherited Density Decimal}
+\label{subsec:rt_historical_rhof_provenance_audit}
+
+\paragraph{Source and status.}
+\textbf{[HISTORICAL ORIGIN / NOT A CURRENT DERIVATION].}
+The early VAM paper registered as \texttt{VAM7-DENSITY-2025} is the traced
+source of the decimal later rounded to
+$\rhoF=7.0\times10^{-7}\,\mathrm{kg\,m^{-3}}$.  The source assigned the
+electron rest energy to a vorticity scale
+\begin{align}
+    \omega_{\rm VAM}
+    =
+    \alpha\omega_c
+    =
+    \alpha\frac{m_ec^2}{\hbar}
+\end{align}
+and to the selected effective volume
+\begin{align}
+    V_{\rm eff}^{\rm VAM}
+    =
+    \frac{r_e^3}{3} .
+\end{align}
+It then formed
+\begin{align}
+    \mathcal J_{\omega}^{\rm VAM}
+    :=
+    \frac{2m_ec^2}{
+        \left(\alpha m_ec^2/\hbar\right)^2
+        \left(r_e^3/3\right)} .
+    \label{eq:rt_vam7_historical_microinertia}
+\end{align}
+Re-evaluation with the present constant chain gives
+\begin{align}
+    \mathcal J_{\omega}^{\rm VAM}
+    \simeq
+    6.84\times10^{-7}\,\mathrm{kg\,m^{-1}},
+\end{align}
+consistent with the historical decimal but not with its stated volumetric
+unit.
+
+\paragraph{Dimensional adjudication.}
+Because
+\begin{align}
+    \left[
+    \frac{m_ec^2}{\omega^2V}
+    \right]
+    =
+    \frac{\mathrm{kg\,m^2\,s^{-2}}}
+         {\mathrm{s^{-2}m^3}}
+    =
+    \mathrm{kg\,m^{-1}},
+\end{align}
+Eq.~\eqref{eq:rt_vam7_historical_microinertia} defines a rotational
+microinertia per volume or an equivalent line-inertia coefficient.  It does
+not define a mass density in $\mathrm{kg\,m^{-3}}$.  The dimensionally
+consistent energy form is
+\begin{align}
+    u_{\omega}
+    =
+    \frac12\mathcal J_{\omega}^{\rm VAM}
+    |\boldsymbol\omega|^2,
+\end{align}
+not $\tfrac12\rhoF|\boldsymbol\omega|^2$.
